e-title>Multidrug resistance in <italic>Salmonell</italic>a <italic>enterica</italic> serotype Typhimurium from humans in France (1993 to 2003).</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source> <year>2006</year>;<volume>44</volume>:<fpage>700</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>8</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/JCM.44.3.700-708.2006</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16517842</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R14"><label>14. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Ribot</surname> <given-names>EM</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Wierzba</surname> <given-names>RK</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Angulo</surname> <given-names>FJ</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Barrett</surname> <given-names>TJ</given-names></string-name> <article-title><italic>Salmonella enterica</italic> serotype Typhimurium DT104 isolated from humans, United States, 1985, 1990, and 1995.</article-title><source>Emerg Infect Dis</source> <year>2002</year>;<volume>8</volume>:<fpage>387</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>91</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11971772</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>